<title>HUNGARY: NEW AUTO SALES IN CENTRAL EUROPE - JANUARY TABLE.</title>
<headline>NEW AUTO SALES IN CENTRAL EUROPE - JANUARY TABLE.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>New auto sales in Central</p>
<p>European Free Trade Agreement (CEFTA) countries rose 19.7</p>
<p>percent to 66,679 units in January 1997 from 55,728 units in</p>
<p>January 1996, according to a Reuters survey.</p>
<p>CEFTA comprises the Czech Republic, Hungary, Poland,</p>
<p>Slovakia and Slovenia. The survey, which Reuters issues</p>
<p>monthly, defines autos as cars, minibuses, off-road vehicles,</p>
<p>pickups, vans and other four-wheeled motor vehicles not over</p>
<p>5.0 tonnes in gross weight.</p>
